00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.030
So lots to talk about so here’s my top 5
moments, careful for spoilers if you haven’t

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.030
seen the episode.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:38.740
Number 5 - Oberyn Martell and Tywin Come To
An Arrangement.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.600
So many important things we learned from this.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.010
Twyin believes in Daenerys dragons and flat
out denies any involvement in the death of

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.290
Oberyn’s sister.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.860
But he only denies knowledge it happened.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.850
Not that someone under him, like say The Mountain,
didn’t do it.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:00.033
So he agrees to arrange a friendly chat between
Oberyn and said Mountain in exchange for sitting

00:01:00.033 --> 00:01:01.033
on Tyrion’s trial.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.033
And the seat on new King Tommen’s small
council.

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:03.400
There’s a small change from the books here.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:12.049
Originally Tyrion had already offered the
seat on the small council in exchange for

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:17.140
Dorne’s help against Stannis during the
Battle of Blackwater.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:24.909
Tywin’s also trying to use Joffrey’s Death
as a way to smooth things out with the Martells.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:31.369
But I can’t wait to see Oberyn meet The
Mountain in combat.

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:36.069
How funny was it when Tywin just burst in
on Oberyn in the middle of that pile of flesh.

00:01:36.069 --> 00:01:39.119
It reminded me of when Tyrion did the same
thing in episode 1.

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:43.190
There’s something about Lannisters walking
in on Oberyn while he’s humping people.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:48.009
But I guess it seems like based on Oberyn’s
speech, he thinks every minute until old age

00:01:48.009 --> 00:01:50.119
should be spent humping your brains out.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:54.960
It was really nice of Twyin to call back to
the Martell’s being the only force to resist

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.869
the Aegon’s Conquest of Westeros.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:05.459
I wonder if George RR Martin released that
Aegon excerpt last week because this shout

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:06.889
out from Tywin was happening in this episode?

00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:08.240
Let me know if you agree.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.010
Number 4 - Littlefinger Helps Sansa Escape

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.020
If you were clueing for looks into the mystery
of Joffrey’s death, I feel like Littlefinger

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.040
would just have a giant red flashing light
on his head.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.480
He doesn’t out right say I was responsible
for everything.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.760
But he did point out the fake necklace and
the fact that Ser Dontos was only doing what

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.690
he told him to do.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:33.450
So it would have had to have all been Littlefinger’s
plan to incriminate Tyrion.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:37.500
Even if the show is doing it differently from
the books, I don’t think it was that simple.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.910
There will probably be more details in the
next episode.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:47.180
Remember this though, Littlefinger always
reminds Sansa that everyone in the capital

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.090
is a liar, then promptly tells her she’s
safe with him and they’re heading home.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:57.400
So right away giant red flashing warning lights
everywhere go off.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.430
There was a clip of them on the boat in the
next episode, so I think they’ll show where

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.710
he’s taking her.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:07.960
Did anyone else feel like Littlefinger was
laying on his Batman voice a little thick?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.580
Who would ever trust someone that talked like
that?

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.770
Number 3 - Daario Vs The Champion of Meereen

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:17.770
So just a few minor changes from the books
because they cut out a few characters but

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:21.540
I thought this was an amazing way to show
off Daario’s skills and humor.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.820
Like when they’re all listing their accomplishments
and Daenerys thinks they’re too precious

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.820
to fight.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.350
So Daario is just like “I’m a nobody,
let me fight him”.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:33.940
I am definitely like the new actor way more
than Ed Skrein, so I can’t wait to see more

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.210
of him when the story picks back up.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.930
Did anyone get a Indiana Jones vibe with the
way he took down the Champion.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.840
Especially with the way he chucked the knife
then turned around to face camera as if it

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.250
was no big deal.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.660
Like in Raiders of the Lost Ark.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.500
High fives to the writers and people that
filmed that scene.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.900
Just awesome all around.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.900
Number 2 - The Siege of Mereen

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.370
If you didn’t catch it right away she catapulted
all the old slaves collars over the wall as

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.910
proof of her intentions.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.500
That she was going to break their chains.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:07.201
They didn’t show a lot of them, but the
quote unquote masters are heads of the big

00:04:07.201 --> 00:04:08.410
slaving families of Meereen.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.820
We’ll probably meet them once Daenerys makes
it inside the walls.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.320
We didn’t get a chance to see the Unsullied
in open combat last season, so seeing them

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.120
in formation launching those barrels was really
cool.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.979
I’ll be interested to see if they change
anything in the next episode.

00:04:21.979 --> 00:04:26.539
I think last season Barristan Selmy called
out Ser Jorah as a liar, but in this episode

00:04:26.539 --> 00:04:29.189
Daenerys called him one of her most trusted
advisors.

00:04:29.189 --> 00:04:34.599
She really laid it on thick, so I wonder if
that means something is going to happen between

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:35.599
them soon.

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:39.819
There were a ton of scenes in the trailer
with them inside the city walls.

00:04:39.819 --> 00:04:43.520
So I don’t think he’s going anywhere anytime
soon.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.150
Their ‘ship is still strong.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.330
Stronger than Jaime and Cersei anyway.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:55.800
Number 1 - Jaime takes Cersei right next to
Joffrey’s Corpse

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.479
I could spend an entire video about the many
things that happened in Baelor’s Sept.

00:05:00.479 --> 00:05:04.129
First off, that was the Sept where Joffrey
just got married last week.

00:05:04.129 --> 00:05:05.819
So that was a little creepy.

00:05:05.819 --> 00:05:09.699
Then the burial rights with the coins on his
face with eyes drawn on.

00:05:09.699 --> 00:05:10.699
Also creepy.

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:13.360
Did you notice how the camera just lingered
on him.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:20.349
I’ll mention Tywin and Tommen during Bonus
moments, but the real moment was Cersei and

00:05:20.349 --> 00:05:21.430
Jaime.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:26.069
I think for the first time I can remember,
she openly calls out Joffrey to Jaime as their

00:05:26.069 --> 00:05:28.729
son and demands he kill Tyrion.

00:05:28.729 --> 00:05:33.139
Then he has his way with her and did you notice
how when they’re in the middle of all that

00:05:33.139 --> 00:05:34.139
awfulness.

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:38.870
Joffrey’s face is clearly visible in the
frame.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:42.009
Let me know if you were not shaking your head
in disgust.

00:05:42.009 --> 00:05:48.370
I love how Game of Thrones does such a good
job of making you uncomfortable.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:53.719
It also kind of seemed like Cersei was the
only one mourning Joffrey.

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:57.310
Even Twyin called him a terrible king when
he was talking to Tommen.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:05:59.800
So here’s a couple bonus moments that we
also need to mention, but I didn’t think

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:03.300
were quite as important as my top 5.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.310
Arya definitely looks like she’s losing
patience with the Hound.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:12.710
I wonder if she’s just going to stick him
with Needle when she gets the chance.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.020
Shireen and Davos’ letter to the Iron Bank
is a huge deal.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.509
Remember the shot of the Titan of Braavos.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.919
That’s a follow up on what’s going on
in this letter.

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:22.410
It’s Davos trying to get more ships and
men for Stannis.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:28.000
I think Mark Gatiss is getting ready to make
his grand entrance.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.060
Sam and Gilly were pretty adorable.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.199
I really want those two to get a happy ending.

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:36.150
But I don’t think anyone on Game of Thrones
is allowed to have a happy ending.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:39.159
I wonder if that’s part of George RR Martin’s
contract.

00:06:39.159 --> 00:06:40.999
No Happy Endings.

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:45.815
Jon, Sam and Maester Aemon seem like the only
truly smart people at the Wall right now.

00:06:45.815 --> 00:06:49.750
But I think they listened to Jon’s warning
about killing the mutinous Night’s Watch

00:06:49.750 --> 00:07:00.400
brothers at Crasters to keep them from helping
Mance.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.780
Either way Ygritte and those Thenn’s look
hungry for Crow.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:11.530
Who else got a Tyrion Pod Sherlock and Watson
vibe.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:17.409
Tyrion was clueing for looks as to who could
have killed Joffrey and who he could call

00:07:17.409 --> 00:07:18.990
on to support him.

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.699
And then the sad goodbye.

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:22.960
Pod, this if Farewell.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:33.900
and Let’s save all the Tommen and Tywin
talk for the comments.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:42.659
Because that speech Twyin gave him was right
out of book 3, pretty much word for word.

00:07:42.659 --> 00:07:48.349
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite WTF moment was.

00:07:48.349 --> 00:07:51.150
Jaime and Cersei or any of the Daenerys Meereen
scenes?

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.099
They were all amazing, it’s hard to pick.

00:07:54.099 --> 00:07:58.259
Overall, another solid A. I kind of worried
I’m going to end up giving all the episodes

00:07:58.259 --> 00:08:00.249
this season an A minus or better.

00:08:00.249 --> 00:08:03.259
So I’ll try to be more critical in the future.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:07.379
But it’s hard to when everything is going
crazy in the best possible way.

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:11.409
I felt like the Sam Gilly scenes were the
weakest, but only because it seems like they’re

00:08:11.409 --> 00:08:16.009
trying to set up a bigger side story for them.

00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:19.139
If you got a creepy vibe from the stable he
took Gilly too you weren’t alone.

00:08:19.139 --> 00:08:21.300
There’s no way she’s going to be safer
there.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.770
I did love Sam’s reaction to “other work”.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.499
Nope, no other work!

00:08:25.499 --> 00:08:28.529
As for the cinematography and all the sets
I feel like I already speechified all my favorites

00:08:28.529 --> 00:08:29.529
already.

00:08:29.529 --> 00:08:31.099
Indiana Jones Daario and all.

00:08:31.099 --> 00:08:34.360
Littlefinger’s ship did kind of remind me
of something from a pirate movie with all

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.789
that fog a silence.

00:08:37.789 --> 00:08:42.839
I’ll only be rewatching it two more times,
tonight.

00:08:42.839 --> 00:08:46.880
Let me know what your final verdict is and
what your big questions are.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:49.770
I’m posting my Q&amp;A video tomorrow night.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.260
And announcing the round 3 giveaway winner.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.430
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:56.520
I think because Bran’s story is back I might
do that Bloodraven bonus video next week.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:09:00.560
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A, I’ll
add the annotation as soon as I post the video

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:04.820
and click here for my Purple Wedding video.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:06.730
Ding Dong the witch is dead.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.510
Thanks for watching everyone, see you tomorrow.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:08.920
High Fives!

